<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16342" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπάθητος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπᾰθάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not struck
				close with the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπάθη</span>: hence, either <i>loosely
				woven</i> or <i>not woven</i> (i. e. of skin), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλαῖνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					877
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>not in close order,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάλαγξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					16.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
